 solving the riddles and  begins engaging the duo in a battle of  minds look actual terrorist protagonists  in all seriousness having such  protagonists opens up several mysteries  such as questions as to why our main  characters ended up becoming extremists  the story behind the two is actually a  lot more tragic than you'd expect  adding to that are moral questions and  some political parallels and the good ol  saying that everything is political  can't be any truer for terror in  resonance and on with amazing music and  animation the show is also filled with  thrilling action that leaves you wanting  more  coming up next at number eight its  garden of sinners now for something  different God loves sinners is a series  of movie starring shecky due to her  upbringing she lives in isolation and so  she encounters ordinary high school  student Mickey ax murders begin  occurring in the city with Shiki  becoming a prime suspect  Mickey o refuses to believe that the  girl he befriended is responsible for  everything despite seeing her on the  site of one such gruesome killing garden  of sinners has this nifty thing where  the story isn't told in order yes they  put a Haruhi on us only a lot more  serious and edgy bewitching ly  captivating and with its unrestrained  violence boldness to tackle mature  issues and an ever-present  air of mystery garden of sinners will be  a draining experience that isn't for the  unprepared but past all of that is one  of the more amazing works in the world  of anime  [Music]  number seven is paranoia agent in  paranoia agent the police are on the  trail of a legendary figure called Shona  bat appearing is a team that wield two  bent baseball bat he sets off to attack  the people in Musashino furthermore his  attacks don't seem random at all as he  only attacks those who fit a certain  category if you're not aware the creator  of this anime is the leisa Toshi khan  known for his mind-bending style that's  putting it kindly in directing vi