 point steins gate goes the next mile  while a car bait deals with tough  choices we get to join the action  grappling with the concepts that the  show presents us theorizing on the fate  of the characters and waiting for the  next major development steins gate has  the magical ability to keep its viewers  completely engaged with every step  making this series the ultimate show to  pick up if you want a mystery anime that  deals with time-travel at number four we  have when they cry a show with cute  girls tagged under mystery thriller then  the girls are chilling and hanging out  in a quiet town setting my hand after  Madoka what could go wrong the second  time around when they cry may seem  unspectacular at first it's the tried  and true visual novel of the main  character ket moving to a province where  he befriends new classmates that look as  if they can conveniently form a harem  the seeming peace and quiet abruptly  ends after he learns about a murder that  happens every few years surely none of  these cute girls that he just prefer  ended can be the ones responsible right  right this anime is unique since its  timelines keep getting reset some people  might think that they're watching some  kind of erased or re0 prototype with a  time-travel shenanigans  overall this animes main selling point  comes from urging the viewers to know  more about the characters you get pulled  into the mystery of how the seemingly  sweetest characters can commit such  heinous acts  [Music]  number three on the list is something  that you should be quite familiar with  the promised Neverland  the promised neverland's a recent series  about the orphanage grace field house  the kids live happily is one big family  under the care of Isabella the mom of  the orphanage after finding out the  truth about the orphanage two of the  smartest kids in there Emma and Norman  begin to lay down the plans from mass  exodus the premise may sound simple  enough but the promised Neverland is as  thrilling as it gets the game of wits is  something to look out for and a lot of  character development unfolds as the  series progresses while the anime  adaption does have its shortcomings its  production especially when it comes to  setting the tone and atmosphere more  than make up for it the promised  Neverland is one hell of a suspenseful  ride keeping viewers on the edge of  their seats as they find out whether the  children can escape the chains of fate  is it any surprise that we have Death  Note at number two in this list Death  Note tells the story of Light Yagami his  life changes when he stumbles upon the  Death Note a notebook with the ability  to kill any person whose name's written  in it recognizing the power that's  fallen into its hands light begins  request of purging the world of  criminals things aren't that easy though  as the police turn their attention to  apprehending the mysterious serial  killer of criminals  enlisting the help of the genius  detective el the game of cat-and-mouse  begins Death Note tries to answer a  whole lot of questions about morals  ethics and justice do criminals really  deserve a second chance  is the world's judicial system flawed  should anyone have the right to take the  lives of other people's into their own  hands for its success death no also  inspired a lot of spin-offs side stories  and even musicals that doesn't even  include the seemingly endless  live-action adaptations and retellings  both great and those that are rather  unflattering  [Music]  finally we have monster taking the  number one spot in a list of top mystery  thriller anime what a way to cap off the  list with the critically acclaimed  masterpiece of now Kiara Sawa monster  tells the story of dr. Kenzo Tenma  a young surgeon disappointed at the  politics and bias within his hospital he  decides to ignore subsequent orders and  operate on a young boy named Johan  Libert saving his life years later to  his surprise he encounters Johann once  more this time as a murderer being  referred to as a monster seeking to fix  his mistake of creating this monster dr.  Tenma goes after Johann when it comes to  mystery thrillers monsters by far one of  the best in terms of setting the tone  and atmosphere for the type of story  that is trying to tell it's without much  of the supernatural elements and  archetypal characters that anime often  takes pride in and it instead works as  an amazing well grounded look at the  human psyche filled to the brim with  suspense deep characters and an  intricate plot that would provoke you  into thinking about life monsters surely  a must watch  well that's it for this video I hope you  can find a show that you really like  among the ones on this list today if  you'd like to recommend some other shows  in the missionary thriller genre then  feel free to do so in the comment  section below don't forget to hit that  like button if you enjoyed the video and  subscribe if you haven't already I'll  see you next time on village you  [Music]

